   "notes": "Downloaded from tanzil.net/pub/download/index.php on 2026-10-06 with parameters quranType=uthmani, outType=txt-2, and every optional symbol switched off (no pause marks, no sajdah signs, no rub-el-hizb signs, no tatweel), after the terms checkbox was ticked on QURRA's behalf with the owner's approval. File SHA-256: bf4f57b968d03f4131c070b1e285da9be0e0a108a21c910e872801ca273312c8 (6,236 ayah lines). The official file prefixes the basmala onto ayah 1 of every surah except 1 and 9 (two spellings: 110 lines use 'بِسْمِ', and 95:1 and 97:1 use 'بِّسْمِ' with an extra shadda in the official file); the raw file keeps it verbatim and data/qurra/ayahs.json separates it as source_prefix. 'Verified' here means the text and its licence terms come from the official source and the Stage 2 pilot was diffed against it (see STAGE_3_REPORT.md); it does not assert any wider commercial clearance beyond the CC BY 3.0 terms. Pause marks are omitted by choice (a Tanzil-supported option) to keep word tokens clean; they can be re-added from a new official download.",
